<BaseLayout title="About"><section class="page-intro" aria-labelledby="about-title"><p class="eyebrow">About</p><h1 id="about-title">A systems-minded approach to AI engineering.</h1><p>I’m {site.fullName}. My work sits where machine learning, operating systems, and hands-on experimentation meet.</p></section><section class="about-profile" aria-label="Professional background"><figure><img src="/assets/raul-cardenas-montoya.jpg" width="960" height="960" alt="Raul Cardenas Montoya" loading="eager" /><figcaption>Systems work, research practice, and durable engineering.</figcaption></figure><div class="prose"><p>I move between agentic engineering, GPU/CUDA work, Rust and Linux systems programming, neuromorphic computing, and FPGA/RTL experimentation. The shared question is practical: what does it take to make a technically ambitious system understandable, repeatable, and useful?</p><p>That perspective puts reproducibility at the center. It shapes how I approach data, experiment setup, tooling, and documentation—not as final polish, but as part of the engineering work itself.</p><p>I am pursuing AI Engineering at Western Governors University while building a practice grounded in careful systems work and public, inspectable artifacts.</p></div></section></BaseLayout>
